Bundled third-party data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The colormaps the renderer offers, and the color names an imported color table
may use, are third-party data compiled into the native addon in bin/, and are
redistributed under their own terms:

  * This product includes color specifications and designs developed by
    Cynthia Brewer (https://colorbrewer.org/). The red–blue and brown–teal
    diverging maps are from ColorBrewer, © Cynthia Brewer, Mark Harrower and
    The Pennsylvania State University, licensed under the Apache License,
    Version 2.0.
  * The turbo colormap is © 2019 Google LLC (Anton Mikhailov), licensed under
    the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  * Viridis, plasma and cividis are from matplotlib and are released into the
    public domain (CC0) by their authors: Nathaniel J. Smith, Stéfan van der
    Walt and Eric Firing (viridis, plasma), and Jamie R. Nuñez, Christopher R.
    Anderton and Ryan S. Renslow (cividis).
  * The cool–warm diverging map is by Kenneth Moreland and is released into the
    public domain (CC0).
  * The color names an imported color table may use are the X11 color database
    (`rgb.txt` from X.Org `app/rgb`), © 1985, 1989, 1998 The Open Group, used
    under the X11 permission notice in that repository's `COPYING`.

The grayscale colormap is a plain black-to-white ramp made here.

